But before editing, inspect config generated file structure around structs to add custom types. Maybe use an extension type in new file? `oc` package spans generated and non-generated files, so we can define new structs in a new file `pkg/config/oc/policy_ext.go`, and add fields to generated structs. But methods Equal etc must be edited to include new fields.

Could also avoid modifying generated `bgp_configs.go` by adding methods? Fields must be in struct. We'll edit.

### API proto modifications

If buf works, add messages:
```
message MatchSourceASSet {
  repeated uint32 source_as_list = 1;
  MatchSet.Type match_set_options = 2; // can't use enum nested? Use MatchSet.Type type
}
message MatchAsPathCommunitySet {
  string as_path_set = 1;
  string community_set = 2;
  repeated uint32 source_as_list = 3;
  MatchSet.Type match_set_options = 4;
  MatchSet.Type as_path_match_set_options = 5;
  MatchSet.Type community_match_set_options = 6;
  MatchSet.Type source_as_match_set_options = 7;
}
```
Add `uint32 priority = 16`? Actually Statement message fields inspect.

